        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="POM01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Earl</roleName>
                        <forename>Thomas William</forename>
                        <surname>Fermor</surname>
                        <addName>Pomfret</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1770-11-22">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1833-06-29"/>
                    <occupation>Soldier, Privy Councillor</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin met him once, in August 1811, spending an evening 
    (I have passed few pleasanter days of my life) in Bognor, talking to Pomfret, 
    the local librarian (Binstead), a General Sturt and a Captain Montgomery - the latter not being named
  in the diary, where Godwin simply writes 'Bonapartian.'  Given Pomfret's later campaigns in the Peninsular War it must have been an interesting evening.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">MS. Abinger c. 42, fols.	65-6: 31 Aug. 1811</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
